# A click on one of the marked moves follows it. It does not play it.
#
# The next-move overlay labels the continuations recorded at the cursor — `3`
# when there is one, `3a` / `3b` / `3c` when there are several. Clicking one is
# the Right arrow with a mouse: the move is already in the tree.
#
# It used to route through playVariationAt(), which starts the match. So
# following the marked move left the phase Playing at a mid-tree cursor, the
# game loop asked the engine for the next move, and GameRecord::move() appended
# the answer as a new child — even though the node already had that move. GNU
# Go being deterministic, the answer *was* the recorded move, so the node ended
# up with two identical children drawn on top of each other and the main line
# acquired a letter it never had: 16, then 16b, then 16c for the same point,
# one per visit. Reported from a real review as "clicking the main variation
# plays it instead of following it".
#
# Black is human and White is the engine, which is the configuration the bug was
# found in: only then is there anybody to answer.

# --- 1. The main line's continuation ------------------------------------------
# simple.sgf is 19x19, B[dd] W[pp] B[dp] W[pd], no result.
load_sgf tests/data/simple.sgf
wait_idle
switch_player black human
switch_player white mock
wait_idle
expect main_line_moves 4
expect at_end true

navigate_back
navigate_back
wait_idle
expect view_position 2
expect at_end false
expect variations 1          # the recorded B[dp], drawn as "3"

# Two clicks, as everywhere: one to take the stone out of the bowl, one to put
# it down — on the marked point this time.
click 3 3
wait_idle
expect holds_stone true
click 3 3
wait_idle

# Followed: the cursor moved and nothing else did.
expect view_position 3
expect move_count 3
expect main_line_moves 4
expect at_end false
expect variations 1          # W[pd] is still ahead, and still the only one
expect holds_stone false
# The regression. This used to be `playing`, and that is the whole bug: nothing
# was played, so nothing may start.
expect phase paused
# Navigation does not edit the SGF, so there is nothing new to save.
expect unsaved_changes false

# Which means the engine has no reason to answer. Waited out rather than
# asserted immediately: a genmove that was going to happen would land here.
wait 1200
wait_idle
expect move_count 3
expect main_line_moves 4
expect phase paused

# And the node we came from still has exactly one child. Two would be the
# duplicate — the same move recorded twice, which is what put a letter on the
# main line.
navigate_back
wait_idle
expect view_position 2
expect variations 1

# Resuming play from a reviewed position is Start's job, and Start is offered:
# White is an engine, it is White's turn, and the game is not over. Same
# division as `play once`, which asks the engine one question without turning
# the review back into a game.
navigate_forward
wait_idle
expect view_position 3
expect phase paused
expect can_start true

# --- 2. A branch that is not the main line ------------------------------------
# variations.sgf has three continuations at move 2: B[dp] (with W[pd] after it),
# B[pd], and a bare B[jj]. Following one must not reorder them either — clicking
# a branch is not a vote for it.
load_sgf tests/data/variations.sgf
wait_idle
switch_player black human
switch_player white mock
wait_idle
navigate_back
navigate_back
wait_idle
expect view_position 2
expect variations 3          # drawn as 3a, 3b, 3c

# The third one, B[jj] at 9,9. It is the one with no continuation, which is what
# makes the check below tell branches apart.
click 9 9
wait_idle
click 9 9
wait_idle
expect view_position 3
expect at_end true           # B[jj] is the end of its line
expect variations 0
expect phase paused
expect unsaved_changes false

# Back out and step forward the ordinary way. Forward always takes the first
# child, so landing on B[dp] — which has a continuation — proves the click left
# the order alone. Had it promoted B[jj], this would be the end of the line.
navigate_back
wait_idle
expect variations 3
navigate_forward
wait_idle
expect view_position 3
expect at_end false
expect variations 1
